  "as_of": "2014-03-04",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would lower Commonwealth election nomination fees for individuals and minor parties by reversing increases introduced through electoral legislation passed in February 2013.",
   "It would halve two nomination amounts in the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918, reducing the sums payable under the two specified paragraphs of that Act.",
   "The changes would begin the day after Royal Assent and apply to elections whose writs were issued on or after the amendments commenced."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "The amount in paragraph 170(3)(a) would fall from $2,000 to $1,000.",
   "The amount in paragraph 170(3)(b) would fall from $1,000 to $500.",
   "A new application rule would link the reduced amounts to the date election writs were issued."
  ],
  "affected": "Individuals and minor parties seeking to contest Commonwealth elections are affected.",
